#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087412 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ec37c5e-8a40-58a7-8af3-4457cd5da43f" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions"}] :question/id #uuid "7826cd52-8603-51ff-902e-c7764639dccd" :question/math-academy-id "e-3666" :question/problem "Express $\\cos^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)} - \\sin^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x = \\cos 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx={\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos^{2} (\\frac{π}{24}) - \\sin^{2} (\\frac{π}{24}) &= \\cos (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{24}) \\\\\n&= \\cos (\\frac{π}{12})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087413 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12ff17ae-9319-5498-a5e0-1d49ddbef50a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Alternative Forms of Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions"}] :question/id #uuid "2b9dc462-ec26-5762-aa64-d9e8f16112c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-3667" :question/problem "Express $2\\cos^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right)}-1$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n2 \\cos^2 x - 1 = \\cos 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx={\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\cos^{2} (\\frac{π}{3}) - 1 &= \\cos (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{3}) \\\\\n&= \\cos (\\frac{2π}{3})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087414 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2902b205-4508-55c6-9a68-f57d3afc9eab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values of Trigonometric Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "e617aaf2-1232-57cc-8644-2467effda030" :question/math-academy-id "e-3668" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\cos^2\\left(22.5^\\circ\\right) - \\sin^2\\left(22.5^\\circ\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x = \\cos 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx={22.5^\\circ}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos^{2} (22.5^{∘}) - \\sin^{2} (22.5^{∘}) &= \\cos (2 \\cdot 22.5^{∘}) \\\\\n&= \\cos 45^{∘} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ec37c5e-8a40-58a7-8af3-4457cd5da43f" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aea59c7-4ab1-557d-bb3b-d1d0c9e5550f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262370} {:answer/id #uuid "c2b65bde-469c-58e0-bd06-c2fe18633322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262371} {:answer/id #uuid "83b02bf6-5f6b-5777-a038-55a1901e61bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262372} {:answer/id #uuid "25d9d878-cf74-5cb7-9d94-4e75ec4289ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262373} {:answer/id #uuid "1edd5c16-fb61-5348-be7f-3dc177df7d8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25d9d878-cf74-5cb7-9d94-4e75ec4289ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262373} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7ce1c18-794c-59f4-bcce-c19d9799a8f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262369}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0194f2b8-4c4e-5a5b-b724-7a12e1903c33" :question/math-academy-id "q-120348" :question/problem "Express $\\sqrt{3}{cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-\\sqrt{3}{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}({cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={35}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {35}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}({cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘})=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ec37c5e-8a40-58a7-8af3-4457cd5da43f" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ea65c2-ca51-5104-87cb-0f807708ebe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262377} {:answer/id #uuid "8c591572-e594-5ddb-90d8-fdc3cd35440f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{cos}⁡{16}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262378} {:answer/id #uuid "753a1fb2-dbab-5233-afe8-2c1ced580e30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{16}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262379} {:answer/id #uuid "7e84e263-4acb-5b21-8ae9-152cc228c9a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262380} {:answer/id #uuid "2ce7abd1-ef56-5a04-b2ca-ec0760df4adf" :answer/type {:db/i